WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.534 --> 00:00:15.275
Bello: Your dad will be back soon, Brad.

2
00:00:15.276 --> 00:00:17.792
Brad: Yeah, any second, I suppose.

3
00:00:17.793 --> 00:00:19.747
Danny: We have to hide Bello!

4
00:00:19.748 --> 00:00:23.177
Bello: I’m not going to hide, Danny.

5
00:00:23.178 --> 00:00:25.979
Tina: You mean you’re going to let my neighbor see you?

6
00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:28.247
Tina: She’ll call the police.

7
00:00:28.248 --> 00:00:31.364
Bello: No, I mean it’s time for me to go back home.

8
00:00:31.365 --> 00:00:32.984
Danny: You’re leaving?

9
00:00:32.985 --> 00:00:36.889
Bello: And quickly. I can’t be caught here.

10
00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:40.016
Tina: I’m going to miss you.

11
00:00:40.017 --> 00:00:42.541
Chuck: We just met you!

12
00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:45.866
Bello: It was a lot of fun to visit your world again.

13
00:00:45.867 --> 00:00:53.459
Bello: I didn’t like being small very much, but it was a great adventure.

14
00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:58.130
Tina: Come on, you guys can say good-bye too.

15
00:00:58.131 --> 00:01:00.859
Dave: How are you going to get back, Bello?

16
00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:06.160
Bello: All it takes is a little magic and a little imagination.

17
00:01:06.161 --> 00:01:12.016
Chuck: Bello, if you could go at any time, why didn’t you leave [n3@when you were in trouble?

18
00:01:12.017 --> 00:01:14.874
Bello: Tina brought me here so that I could help.

19
00:01:14.875 --> 00:01:18.136
Bello: I couldn’t leave until everything was all right.

20
00:01:18.137 --> 00:01:22.673
Bello: Now, I think everything is better than it was before.

21
00:01:22.674 --> 00:01:26.172
Bello: Danny, do you have any nano-putty left?

22
00:01:26.173 --> 00:01:29.130
Danny: I don’t know.

23
00:01:29.131 --> 00:01:31.032
Tina: Here’s some.

24
00:01:31.033 --> 00:01:38.826
Bello: Good. When Danny, Tina, and Brad first came [n3@to my world, they used magic clay.

25
00:01:38.827 --> 00:01:41.894
Bello: It looked a lot like this nano-putty.

26
00:01:41.895 --> 00:01:44.046
Chuck: Magic clay?

27
00:01:44.047 --> 00:01:45.086
Bello: Yes.

28
00:01:45.087 --> 00:01:51.927
Bello: When they used the clay and their imaginations, they were [n3@able to go on a magical journey.

29
00:01:51.928 --> 00:01:55.111
Dave: I’d love to hear the story of your adventures.

30
00:01:55.112 --> 00:01:57.659
Danny: I’m sure I can tell you one day.

31
00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:02.997
Danny: You see, first, we had to make a key from the magic clay—

32
00:02:02.998 --> 00:02:07.901
Bello: Do you mean a key like this one?

33
00:02:07.902 --> 00:02:10.710
Mrs. Rice: Ahh!

34
00:02:10.711 --> 00:02:13.960
Bello: Good-bye, everyone. Take care.

35
00:02:13.961 --> 00:02:24.456
The kids: Good-bye, Bello.

36
00:02:24.457 --> 00:02:26.990
Mrs. Rice: There! You saw it too!

37
00:02:26.991 --> 00:02:29.206
Mr. Joseph: Where did that flashlight go?

38
00:02:29.207 --> 00:02:32.359
It must be here somewhere.

39
00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:35.217
Brad: We must have blown another fuse, Dad.

40
00:02:35.218 --> 00:02:41.987
Mr. Joseph: I’m almost losing my patience, Brad.

41
00:02:41.988 --> 00:02:44.947
Mrs. Rice: Where’s the . . . but there was a . . .

42
00:02:44.948 --> 00:02:47.569
Mrs. Rice: I could have sworn I saw a . . .

43
00:02:47.570 --> 00:02:49.267
Mr. Joseph: We must have imagined it.

44
00:02:49.268 --> 00:02:52.522
There’s no such thing as giants.

45
00:02:52.523 --> 00:02:55.044
Mr. Joseph: It’s quite messy in here, Brad.

46
00:02:55.045 --> 00:02:57.845
Brad: Sorry, Dad. We’ll clean it up.

47
00:02:57.846 --> 00:03:02.062
We were just playing.
